longside resolution rate.\n\n**GPU note:** the official competition harness owns model inference and vLLM configuration. This notebook only checks visible hardware and records telemetry; it does not launch a second inference server or claim that CPU-based localization code uses the GPU.\n\n**Environment:** use the competition-configured Kaggle runtime, attach the official competition data and documented wheelhouse, accept competition rules, and ensure the required sandbox is supported. Do not install arbitrary replacements for the official harness.","metadata":{}},{"id":"c0516d77","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Revision notes — controller ablation and benchmark validity\n\nThis revision strengthens the failure-driven adaptive repair experiment rather than claiming that prompt text alone proves a controller works.\n\n- **Matched primary comparison:** E2 (`E2_forgex_no_controller`) is the base agent with no failure-driven controller section; E4 (`E4_failure_controller`) adds only the controller policy to that same base prompt. The model, tools, task IDs, sandbox, and budgets must be identical.\n- **Combined comparison:** E5 combines evidence-fusion localization and the controller. E3 adds localization only. These are prompt-policy ablations, not separately trained models and not a claim that Python helper functions execute inside the harness.\n- **Operational controller protocol:** the E4/E5 prompts require a compact attempt ledger with hypothesis, evidence, action, result, failure class, cost, and next step; failure classes map to different next actions; repeated failed actions require new evidence; retry limits and regression handling are explicit.\n- **No false completion:** an arm is valid only if the harness exits successfully, no infrastructure failure is detected, task IDs are unique and exactly match the selected set, and each task has a recognized resolution outcome. A file containing five rows is not proof of a completed experiment.\n- **Paired effect reporting:** compare E4 against E2 on the same task IDs, report wins/losses/ties, paired effect size, a bootstrap confidence interval, and an exact two-sided McNemar test when available. Never treat infrastructure failures as unresolved bugs.\n- **No automatic scientific claim:** if the harness, task outcomes, or paired coverage is invalid, the report explicitly blocks the resolution-improvement claim.\n\nThis notebook has not been executed against the official harness by the editing process. The revised cells add safeguards and experimental design; they cannot manufacture successful benchmark outcomes.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"3fcf9a6e","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 0. Setup\nPaths are discovered under `/kaggle/input` or taken from `FORGEX_*` environment variables.","metadata":{}},{"id":"41c1138b-901f-4df3-922d-fc084c783498","cell_type":"code","source":"# Safe dependency preflight. Avoid upgrading torch/transformers in the competition runtime.\nimport importlib.metadata as _md\nfor _dist in (\"torch\", \"transformers\", \"accelerate\", \"pandas\"):\n    try:\n        print(f\"{_dist}: {_md.version(_dist)}\")\n    except _md.PackageNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"{_dist}: NOT INSTALLED\")\nprint(\"If a required dependency is missing, use only the competition-provided offline wheelhouse and documented versions.\")\n","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-27T17:24:12.969358Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-27T17:24:12.969539Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-27T17:24:12.992846Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-27T17:24:12.96952Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-27T17:24:12.992348Z"},"trusted":true},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"torch: 2.11.0+cu128\ntransformers: 5.16.1\naccelerate: 1.14.0\npandas: 2.3.3\nIf a required dependency is missing, use only the competition-provided offline wheelhouse and documented versions.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":1},{"id":"ced1fb1f-3fe5-4ae4-9e9d-10c4f71edebc","cell_type":"code","source":